// Plugin: no-form-state-in-useeffect
// Severity: warn
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Catches:    `useEffect(fn, [...])` whose dependency array references TanStack
//             Form state — `form.state.values`, `form.store`, or any
//             `<x>.state.values` / `<x>.store` (catches renamed `form` bindings).
//
// Rationale:  Pre-listener-API anti-pattern. Subscribing to `form.state.values`
//             via React state re-renders the WHOLE COMPONENT on every keystroke
//             and can clobber unsaved typing on a background refetch. Use
//             form-level `listeners.onChange` with `onChangeDebounceMs` instead:
//               • knows WHICH field changed (`fieldApi.name`/`fieldApi.state.value`)
//               • debounces natively (no useDebouncedValue wrapper)
//               • runs in the form lifecycle, not React's render cycle
//               • doesn't re-render the surrounding component
//
// Skips:      Field-level effects inside `<form.Field>` — those receive a
//             `field` arg and re-render only the field block. `form.Subscribe`
//             blocks — the right pattern for UI-only reactivity.
//
// Suppress:   // biome-ignore lint/plugin/no-form-state-in-useeffect: <reason>
//             (rare — one-time seed effects with a documented `form.state.isDirty`
//             guard are the only expected case)
//
// Refs:       src/client/AGENTS.md §5.2 (listeners), §5.5 (Subscribe)
//             features/characters/components/character-form-context.tsx
//             — the canonical listener-driven mirror
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// GritQL note: the snippet `useEffect($_, [$deps])` matches a call with two args
// where the second is an array literal. `$deps` binds to the array's element
// list. `$deps <: contains or { ... }` walks the dep-array subtree and matches
// any literal reading form-state. (No `bubble` needed — the inner `or` arms
// don't bind metavariables that get reused across matches.)

language js

`useEffect($_, [$deps])` as $effect where {
  $deps <: contains or {
    `form.state.values`,
    `form.store`,
    `$_.state.values`,
    `$_.store`
  },
  register_diagnostic(span=$effect, message="`useEffect` reading `form.state.values` / `form.store` in its dep array is the pre-listener anti-pattern: re-renders the whole component on every keystroke and can clobber unsaved typing on a refetch. Use form-level `listeners.onChange` with `onChangeDebounceMs` (AGENTS.md §5.2) — it knows which field changed and runs in the form lifecycle, not the render cycle. For UI-only reactivity, use `form.Subscribe` (AGENTS.md §5.5).", severity="error")
}
